## 🔍 Detailed Tool Comparison

### Playwright MCP

**Installation:**
```bash
npx -y @playwright/mcp
```

**Core Tools:**
```javascript
// Navigation
browser_navigate(url, waitFor?)

// Interaction
browser_click(ref)           // Element from snapshot
browser_doubleClick(ref)
browser_type(ref, text, submit?)
browser_select_option(ref, values)
browser_hover(ref)
browser_drag(from_ref, to_ref)

// XY fallbacks (when DOM fails)
browser_mouse_click_xy(x, y)
browser_mouse_drag_xy(from_x, from_y, to_x, to_y)
browser_mouse_move_xy(x, y)

// Execution
browser_evaluate(script)     // Run JS globally
browser_evaluate(ref, script) // Run JS on element

// Optional caps (flags)
browser_pdf_save(path)       // Requires --caps=pdf
browser_generate_locator(ref) // Requires --caps=testing
```

**Flags:**
```bash
--allowed-hosts=localhost    # Security: limit hosts
--caps=pdf                   # Enable PDF tools
--caps=testing              # Enable locator generation
```

**Strengths:**
- ✅ Deterministic (accessibility tree, no vision)
- ✅ Fast execution (structured data)
- ✅ Stable locators via testing cap
- ✅ PDF generation
- ✅ JS execution
- ✅ XY mouse as fallback

**Weaknesses:**
- ❌ Not designed for discovery
- ❌ No autonomous retry
- ❌ Manual tab management
- ❌ Limited anti-bot features

**Best For:**
- Cached pattern execution
- Form automation with known fields
- PDF generation
- JS evaluation
- Locator validation

